  "paper": "paper_2",
  "question": {
    "html": "<section class=\"context\"><p>A flywheel of radius <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"R=0.15 m\"></span> and mass <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"M=1.8 kg\"></span> rotates around the central axis. The moment of inertia of the flywheel is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{1}{2}MR^{2}\"></span>. A thread is wrapped around the flywheel and a time-varying force <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"F\"></span> is applied to the thread.</p>\n<p><figure data-asset-id=\"fig_01\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 1\" src=\"asset:fig_01\"/></figure></p>\n<p>The angular velocity of the flywheel increases from 4.0 rad s<sup>−1</sup> to 9.0 rad s<sup>−1</sup> in a time of 0.24 s.</p></section><section class=\"question-part\" data-label=\"a\"><p><strong>a</strong> Calculate the angular impulse delivered to the flywheel during the acceleration. [2]</p></section><section class=\"question-part\" data-label=\"b\"><p><strong>b</strong> Determine the average magnitude of <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"F\"></span>. [2]</p></section><section class=\"question-part\" data-label=\"c\"><p><strong>c</strong> State two assumptions of your calculation in part (b). [2]</p></section>"
